  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.7.1 is a security release: upgrade if you use entitlements.\n\n      - **Entitled tables are barriers:** a condition put round an entitled table is evaluated only on the rows the policy admits. Before, an error could quote a value of a row the principal was not shown, and whether a statement failed could reveal whether such a row existed. A security advisory on the repository describes it. A condition that cannot raise, an ORDER BY on columns, joins, aggregates and bounds still reach the source and its indexes; a condition that can raise now runs locally over the admitted rows.\n      - **CASE:** a branch runs only for the rows that take it, so CASE WHEN x <> 0 THEN y / x END guards the division.\n      - **Planner clients:** engines may share one; it is disposed with the last of them, and an engine made on a client already disposed that way is refused when it is made.\n      - **Licence:** the package carries the Elastic License 2.0 text; earlier packages named an empty licence file.\n      - **Compatibility:** no change to the API surface, the protocol or the IR. The barrier is the planner's, which ships inside this package.\n\n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.7.1",
